  "review": "The helper specializes the existing Jones natural-zero theorem using witness positivity, the compiler degree and normalization theorems, and the polynomial identity. Three existing correctness theorems delegate to it; declarations, data and imports are otherwise unchanged. Original snapshots match the source commit parent and final snapshots match the source commit. The 16 source graph pins and import edges, 20 recorded successful commands, log hashes and output object hashes were independently verified. Eight comparable baseline and final target/client/check/axiom logs are identical; all 58 old reports match. The new helper uses the standard three axioms. No warnings were emitted.",
  "limitations": [
    "Four affected prerequisites were freshly rebuilt; other local project and external dependencies remained precompiled. This is not a full dependency-closure or whole-project build.",
    "An initial all-trans trial was reported to time out after 90 seconds; its log is empty, its source was later overwritten, and no standalone machine-readable exit-status record was retained. The adopted proof uses rw instead.",
    "The new-helper axiom probe has a retained source and output but no separate machine-readable status record.",
    "Build timings were taken under concurrency and do not establish a performance trend.",
    "Compiled objects and overlay links are excluded; recorded hashes and sizes remain in phase records."
  ]
